A quick final reminder ahead of July 15th: We’re making a key adjustment to OSDs on Astraeos to address a bug. Starting July 15th, when an OSD lands, it will now destroy any nearby player-built structures within its impact radius. This will be the same radius used for OSDs on Extinction.

If you’ve built near potential OSD drop zones, we strongly recommend relocating your base before the patch goes live.

]

We’ve rolled out a potential fix for a bug that caused sudden FPS drops due to VRAM allocation issues. This update also reverts the temporary workaround introduced in v67 (June 20), which dynamically managed VRAM to reduce memory buildup.
We’ll be actively monitoring player reports to confirm if this resolves the issue—if not, we’ll continue working toward a more permanent solution.

